  "scope": "Captured default-off measurement report Y coordinates; source point/midpoint and sampling area/COM/rectangle ownership. Physical world geometry and disabled numerical results stay unchanged. No new runtime code dependency, model, font or asset.",
  "contract": {
    "api": "TargetAnalysisOptions.invert_y=false; owned C++ optional TargetAnalysisPlane.reported_y, reported_center_of_mass_y, reported_bounding_y, exposed read-only in Python. Existing *_world, bounding_y, rectangle vectors, Feret, scalar statistics, X/Z and stored calibration are unchanged.",
    "setting": "measurement_invert_y: Boolean=false; shared native/Python Settings, Measurements > Invert Y coordinates. Captured before launch; publication refuses a consumed setting change. Existing column choices are preserved.",
    "calibration": "An already axis-reversed world Y basis (direction[3]==direction[5]==0, direction[4]<0) remains upward: calibration and option use OR semantics. Otherwise nonzero world origin Y reports -worldY; zero origin uses (height-1)*spacingY-worldY. Source frame/height for points and line midpoints; sampling frame/height for area centroid, COM and bounding origin. Exact nonzero-origin zero is canonical original +0, rather than the -0 produced by simply negating worldY.",
    "native_extension": "For a non-axis-aligned native affine, this is an explicit report-only world-Y scalar reflection with the same anchor. It is analytically qualified, not an ImageJ rotated-world-coordinate claim. Physical geometry and X/Z stay fixed.",
    "original_policy": "Observed option changes Y/YM/BY only, not Feret coordinates/angles or scalar/ellipse outputs. Irregular-line/angle zero-coordinate rows remain zero. Existing unsupported point/line auxiliary columns retain their M3/T06 owners.",
    "timing_resources": "Fixed three optional doubles are charged by sizeof(TargetAnalysisPlane) in existing result/working estimates. Existing JSON keys are replaced, not appended as image data. No additional buffer, source-plane traversal, provider read or processing controller. Runtime cap refusal precedes checkpoint/provider access. Nonfinite numerical summaries remain valid without weakening geometry conversion.",
    "provenance": "v21 only when invert_y requested; prior versions/defaults remain compatible. Detached scalar results retain no new source/provider ownership.",
    "persistence_output": "Both hosts use the same native row serializer/formatting and shared Copy CSV/Save CSV path. Original and report aliases are explicit: visible Y/centroid_y, YM and BY prefer reported fields. Preferences and workspace rows round-trip. Clipboard check uses a restored owned ImGui sink; OS interoperability remains open."
  },
